</table></div><div class="prose"><h3>Notes to the table (condensed)</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Regular, benchmark [a].</strong> EER %, FRLL families in the order FaceMorpher / OpenCV / AMSL / WebMorph, each against the 204 FRLL genuine photos (102 persons). MAD22 FaceMorpher is against the 185 MAD22 genuine photos (byte copies of FRLL photos); every MAD22 number is on our 185 + 4,069 MAD22 files, against the published 204 + 4,483. A12.4 calls the recipes' benchmark pool "an eval-pipeline diagnostic, never a detection result".</li>
<li><strong>Regular, controlled [b].</strong> E7 shrinking factors: FRLL FM 1.47x, OCV 1.56x, AMSL and WebMorph 1.80x, MAD22 FaceMorpher 3.30x. MAD22 OpenCV and Webmorph are left out (~1.0x, so E7 tests nothing there). Person-clustered 95% CIs (A41 S3): SelfMAD FRLL FM 4.8 [1.95, 7.34] and OCV 3.9 [1.41, 5.85]; ViT-B/16 FRLL FM 4.42 [2.12, 6.93] and OCV 4.42 [2.08, 7.37]; MAD22 FM SelfMAD 0.11 [0.00, 0.89] and ViT-B/16 5.94 [3.25, 10.62].</li>
<li><strong>H1 label rule</strong> (A36 amendment 1). "Above the floor" needs a point margin D ≥ +0.05, a one-sided Bonferroni lower bound of D &gt; 0, and a seed-CI lower bound of AUC − floor &gt; 0. Labels on the 11 primary rows are registered; the others are descriptive; all were set post-freeze. The SelfMAD own-crop <code>orig</code> 0.872 and <code>pp</code> 0.821 are point estimates.</li>
<li><strong>GAN, benchmark [c].</strong> MIPGAN-I is EER % on MAD22 MIPGAN-I (generator PNG against camera JPEG). ViT-B/16 18.4 [13.4, 23.6] and ViT-L/14 11.9 [8.0, 15.6] (person 95%, DC-8). The G-test is held-out StyleGAN2 latent-average morphs of FEI pairs against FEI frontal captures; its morphs are scaled to the genuine photos' face size by construction. C4: "These sets compare generator output (PNG) with camera photos (JPEG)."</li>
<li><strong>GAN, controlled [d].</strong> H3 floors: bytes 0.526, eye geometry 0.560, combined covariates 0.607–0.617; "reversed" means the 95% pair CI lies below 0.5. A row would count as "shown" only if H3 is above its combined floor by its CI and X4 is above 0.5 by its CI. No row meets this: the highest H3 is M2 at 0.591 [pair 90% 0.572, 0.610], the highest X4 is M4 at 0.517 [95% 0.493, 0.541].</li>
<li><strong>Diffusion, benchmark [e].</strong> EER on the FRLL diffusion families against the original genuine photos. Recipes show UA8c: the mean EER over the seven held-out diffusion families, each capped at 50. The cap hides inversion, so the uncapped UA8 under E7 is shown beside it.</li>
<li><strong>Diffusion, controlled [f].</strong> Person-clustered 95% CIs exist only for the SelfMAD own-crop, SelfMAD our-pipeline, ViT-B/16, ViT-L/14 and FE ViT-L/14 releases. X3 values are Greedy-DiM / MorDIFF unless a family is named; the Greedy-DiM vs reconstruction comparison is floor-limited (file bytes alone 0.987–0.998). H2 (IP-Adapter-FaceID SD 1.5; floors 0.522 / 0.518) and Arc2Face (every row 0.482–0.539) are descriptive.</li>
</ul></div><div class="prose"><h3>Verdict rules (post hoc, not A41 grades)</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Regular.</strong> <em>holds</em>: under E7 the EER is ≤ 10% on at least two FRLL landmark families and no FRLL landmark family or MAD22 FaceMorpher rises by more than 3 points, <strong>and</strong> H1 <code>orig</code> is labelled above its floor. <em>partly holds</em>: exactly one of the two. <em>does not hold</em>: neither. Descriptive tags: <em>inverted natively</em> (native EER above 50% on at least two FRLL landmark families), <em>weak natively</em> (≥ 25% on all four, not inverted), <em>collapses under E7</em> (a family at ≤ 35% natively rises by at least 10 points).</li>
<li><strong>GAN.</strong> <em>shown / not shown</em>, as in [d]. Every row is "not shown". It does not mean the detector is blind to two identities.</li>
<li><strong>Diffusion.</strong> E7 "holds" on a family when the E7 EER is within 5 points of native and at most 25%. <em>holds</em>: E7 holds on at least one family and H2 or Arc2Face is clearly above its floor (no row qualifies). <em>partly holds</em>: E7 holds on at least one family. <em>does not hold</em>: on no family. X3 is left out of the verdicts: its positive control failed, and C2 calls the one separating row "open".</li>
</ul></div><div class="tw"><table class="small">
