<h3>Status of the numbers</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Registered decision cells.</strong> SelfMAD MAD22 FaceMorpher under E7 (F4 (i), supported); ViT-B/16 FRLL FaceMorpher under E7 (F4 (ii)); SelfMAD Greedy-DiM and MorDIFF (C1, "strong (final)"); ViT-B/16 MorDIFF (C2, "descriptive row (final)"; the refuter F7 fired); ViT-L/14 Greedy-DiM as the negative control (F4 (iii), supported); FE ViT-L/14 as the X3 positive-control gate (failed, 0.636 ≤ 0.65).</li>
<li><strong>Registered tests.</strong> H3 and X4 on the ‡ rows: C3, "strong (narrow)". Claim B: "meets its registered criterion". C4: "construction sentence".</li>
<li><strong>Registered labels without a grade.</strong> The H1 <code>orig</code> labels on the 11 primary rows; H4b through A36 H-new-72 ("neither"); renders vs camera, H-new-83 ("neither"); "CLIP carries the render cue", H-new-84 ("neither").</li>
<li><strong>Everything else is descriptive</strong>, including every verdict word, every <code>pp</code> H1 label and every recipe number. A41's rules were written after earlier estimates on the same questions had been seen; never call A41 "confirmatory".</li>
</ul></div>
</section>
<section class="s" id="s3">
<h2><span class="n">3</span>Shortcut per method, against the registered bar</h2>
<div class="prose"><p>The comparison table says how each detector does under the controls. This section asks the stricter question: for each method, was a shortcut found under A41's registered rules, and how far does the evidence go?</p></div><div class="prose"><h3>The registered bar (A41)</h3>
<p>The program's registered bar is A41's. The top grade a shortcut claim can earn is "meets registered criteria N1–N4", and all four conditions are required. A grade is the label A41's registered rules assign, not a level of certainty (CONCLUSIONS).</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>N1, reliance.</strong> A control removes the construction difference while everything else stays fixed, and at least half of the separation goes.<ul>
<li>In numbers (CONCLUSIONS' summary): the benchmark error rate (EER) is at most 10%; the person-clustered lower bound of its rise under the control is at least +10 points; at least half of the separation is gone (d′ share ≥ 0.5).</li>
<li>Operationally (F1, F2, F5): the rise is decided by a one-sided person-clustered test that it exceeds +10, at its Holm level (p10 ≤ level), not by the printed two-sided interval. C2's printed interval starts at 10.3 (one-sided lower bound 10.97), but p10 0.0170 &gt; 0.00833, so tier 2 was not reached.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>N2, specificity (F4).</strong> The same control leaves real morph evidence detectable: MAD22 FaceMorpher morphs stay detected under it. It also does not move a detector that ignores downsampling: the ViT-L/14 release, on Greedy-DiM. This shows only that E7 does not mechanically destroy a detector that is good on DiM (A41's printed caveat).</li>
<li><strong>N3, validity in kind (F3, X3 only).</strong> Genuine photos passed through the morphs' own generator family, without any morphing, behave like morphs for the detector. Here these are DiffAE reconstructions (X3). The test must also show that it could catch identity mixing at all: its positive-control detector, FE ViT-L/14, must score above 0.65 on the reconstructions.</li>
<li>
<p><strong>N4, reproduction.</strong> For C1, with the release's own crop on the raw files (X7′, H-new-145), both components:</p>
<ul>
<li>"published regime reproduced on raw files": raw Greedy-DiM within 5 points of the published 7.60, and the FRLL-5 mean within 5 of 2.96;</li>
<li>"our frames do not change the native regime": |raw − frame| ≤ 3 points for Greedy-DiM and MorDIFF.</li>
</ul>
<p>The raw-file reversal is descriptive. For C2, N4 is the five-crop check (X14b, F6).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>No claim meets this bar.</strong> The closest is C1, the SelfMAD release on diffusion morphs:</p>
<ul>
<li>It meets N1 (F1, F2), N2 (F4, Greedy-DiM; not shown on MorDIFF) and N4 (X7′, both components).</li>
<li>It does not meet N3: the positive control reached only 0.636.</li>
<li>A border or alignment artefact of our control photos is not formally excluded.</li>
<li>The top grade would also need no fired C1 kill and W-c resolved (PROTOCOL l.14441).</li>
<li>So its grade is "strong (final)", and the top grade cannot be reached.</li>
</ul></div><div class="callout"><p><strong>Three statements that are easy to confuse.</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>"The result meets A41's shortcut definition."</strong> This is about what carries one detector's result on one benchmark cell. A41's definition requires, in numbers:</p>
<ol>
<li>a construction difference separates morphs from genuine photos;</li>
<li>the same difference can be put into genuine photos without any morphing;</li>
<li>removing it removes at least half of the separation, at the thresholds above.</li>
</ol>
<p>C1 is the only claim whose numbers meet A41's shortcut definition. It is graded "strong (final)", and two registered conditions are open: the assay sensitivity of X3, and a pool artefact that is not formally excluded. In plain words (CONCLUSIONS): the SelfMAD release treats genuine photos that were merely shrunk to the morphs' face size as more morph-like than real Greedy-DiM morphs.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>"The benchmark number changes under a control."</strong> The benchmark number changes when a control alters a construction difference. This says neither by how much deployed performance is overstated nor that the detector relies on that difference.</p>
<ul>
<li>A41's "inflated" label (tier 1) needs a native EER of at most 10% and a one-sided person-clustered test that the rise exceeds +5 passing at its Holm level (p5). It was first printed for the ViT-B/16 release on MorDIFF. It was superseded by "descriptive row" when a registered refuter fired, so this note does not use the word for that row.</li>
<li>Every other rise under a control below is descriptive. No registered rule was applied to it. Person intervals exist only for the A41 S2 and S3 release cells, not for FE ViT-B/16, FS, MixFaceNet-MAD or the recipes.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>"The detector fails a clean test."</strong> This is an absence. On a set where both classes come from the same tool or generator, and the known remaining differences are named (H1 file size, floor 0.620; H3 latent spread, by construction; H4b file size, floor 0.912), the detector does not rank morphs above non-morphs by a useful margin.<ul>
<li>What it shows (C3 only, StyleGAN3): the detector's GAN benchmark number is not evidence of morph detection. The H1 labels are registered without a grade; H2 and Arc2Face are descriptive.</li>
<li>What it does not show: a shortcut, because it says nothing about which cue the detector uses on the benchmark. Nor does it show that the detector is blind to identity, unless the test has power and a passing positive control. X4 sits near 0.5 by construction, H2 is low-potency, and X3's positive control failed.</li>
<li>The registered example is C3, "strong (narrow)", for GAN morphs.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Claims B and C4 describe the benchmarks, not the detectors:</p>
<ul>
<li>B: morph and genuine files differ in construction attributes.</li>
<li>C4: the GAN sets compare generator output with camera photos.</li>
</ul>
<p>They make a shortcut possible. They do not show that any detector uses one.</p></div><div class="prose"><h3>Reading the table</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>E7.</strong> Genuine photos shrunk to the morphs' median face size before the same alignment. Cells give EER in %, native → E7.</li>
<li><strong>Brackets.</strong> [ ] is a person-clustered 95% interval unless marked otherwise. "pair 90%" marks the A36 H1 and H3 intervals. Row 11's FRLL reproduction interval is marked "TOST": the A12-BR TOST interval (90%) over seeds plus the image bootstrap.</li>
<li><strong>X3 AUC.</strong> Published morphs against DiffAE reconstructions of the genuine photos. Below 0.5 means the reconstructions look more morph-like than the morphs.</li>
<li><strong>"Renders vs camera"</strong> (in the outcome column, not N3). AUC of the single-person StyleGAN3 renders of H3 against FRLL / FFHQ / FEI camera photos (A36 amendment 1, H-new-83).<ul>
<li>The registered cell is the FRLL pool on the 11 primary rows (M1–M8O and the ViT-B/16 and ViT-L/14 releases), with verdict "neither". The FFHQ and FEI pools are descriptive, and so are rows 4–8 and the SelfMAD row (A39 R3).</li>
<li>It is not A41's N3 (A41: "X3 only"). The renders are not re-rendered genuine photos, and StyleGAN3 is not the MIPGAN generator.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>"‡".</strong> One of the 12 primary rows of C3.</li>
<li><strong>Fixed outcome tags.</strong> "meets A41's shortcut definition" (C1 only); "registered refuter fired" (C2); "negative control"; "not tested under a registered rule (descriptive: …)"; "no native EER ≤ 10% to carry" (rows 15–17: "no native EER ≤ 10% that E7 changes").</li>
<li><strong>"Which morph type".</strong> Filled only for cells with a registered grade; "—" otherwise.</li>
<li><strong>"Met / not met".</strong> Used only where A41 registered that condition for that cell. Everything else is a logged number with its status.</li>
<li><strong>GAN status.</strong> "C3 absence, 'strong (narrow)'; not a shortcut grade" on every ‡ row.</li>
</ul></div><div class="tw"><table class="sc">
<thead>
<tr>
<th>#</th>
<th>Method (networks)</th>
<th>Shortcut test outcome and construction cue (plain words)</th>
<th>Which morph type</th>
<th>N1 reliance (number)</th>
<th>N2 specificity (number)</th>
<th>N3 validity in kind (number)</th>
<th>N4 reproduction (number)</th>
<th>Status (registered grade if any)</th>
<th>Missing for the top grade or replication / next test</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr class="grp"><td colspan="10">Official releases</td></tr>
<tr>
<td>1</td>
<td>SelfMAD release, HRNet-W18, its own dlib crop and resize on our frames (1) ‡</td>
<td><strong>Diffusion: meets A41's shortcut definition (C1).</strong> Against photos shrunk to the morphs' face size before the same alignment (E7), genuine photos score as more morph-like than published Greedy-DiM and MorDIFF morphs. Photos only resampled by DiffAE's aligner, and DiffAE reconstructions, also score above MorDIFF morphs. Cue word: "bona fide processing history; cue not identified". Its score rises with the shrinking factor: photo-only AUC 0.584 at ~1.0x → 0.998 at 3.30x ("dose response", registered secondary rule). <strong>Regular:</strong> not tested under a registered rule (descriptive: AMSL 2.9 → 33.3, WebMorph 5.9 → 51.9). <strong>GAN:</strong> C3 absence (Status). Renders vs camera 1.000 / 0.952 (FRLL / FFHQ; descriptive, A39 R3).</td>
<td>Diffusion: FRLL Greedy-DiM (main cell), MorDIFF (supporting)</td>
<td>Greedy-DiM 8.4 → 90.7, +82.4 [77.3, 87.4], d′ share 2.11. MorDIFF 2.5 → 61.3, +58.8 [54.2, 64.6], d′ share 1.19 (F1, F2 supported). <strong>Met:</strong> the ranking reverses (share 2.11). The control does more than remove the separation, which the review reads as pointing to the E7 construction (H-new-233, proposed); hence the pool-artefact qualifier.</td>
<td>MAD22 FaceMorpher against its own E7 pool 0.11 [0.00, 0.89]. ViT-L/14 release on Greedy-DiM Δ 0.00 [−3.15, 3.41] (F4 supported). <strong>Met for Greedy-DiM.</strong> On MorDIFF the same control moves ViT-L/14 by +10.74 [7.22, 14.19], so not shown there.</td>
<td>Reconstructions ranked above published morphs: Greedy-DiM 0.024 [0.011, 0.042] (floor-limited), MorDIFF 0.330 [0.284, 0.374]. Resampled-only photos 0.004 / 0.092 (F3 supported). The binding positive control failed: FE ViT-L/14 0.636 [0.579, 0.693] ≤ 0.65. <strong>Not met</strong> ("assay sensitivity not shown").</td>
<td>Raw files with its own crop (X7′, H-new-145). "Published regime reproduced on raw files" (raw Greedy-DiM within 5 of 7.60; FRLL-5 mean within 5 of 2.96): Greedy-DiM 6.39 [3.35, 9.42]; FRLL-5 5.55. "Our frames do not change the native regime" (|raw − frame| ≤ 3): Greedy-DiM 6.39 vs 8.37; MorDIFF 1.49 vs 2.53. <strong>Met</strong> (both components). The reversal persists on the raw files, 6.4 → 87.2 (descriptive).</td>
<td><strong>C1 "strong (final)"</strong>; top grade unreachable. Pool artefact not formally excluded (the border test, XA3c, ran but could not be evaluated). Earlier registered test (A32 H1): "neither". GAN: C3 absence, "strong (narrow)"; not a shortcut grade.</td>
<td>N3 with a positive control that passes. A successor border/alignment test. A second checkpoint, or a retrain over seeds (H-new-242; retrained networks are ours, not the release). Fresh data and another studio pool (X8).</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>2</td>
<td>MADation release, CLIP ViT-B/16 + LoRA (1) ‡</td>
<td><strong>Diffusion: registered refuter fired (C2).</strong> Its MorDIFF EER rises against shrunk photos (C2's registered cue word "fine-detail softness"; cue not identified). But it separates the published MorDIFF morphs from DiffAE reconstructions, a registered refuter: "Identity evidence or a file/frame property: open." Also descriptive, not registered decision cells (F5 covers MorDIFF only; no d′ share logged): DiM-C 6.39 → 29.51, +23.12 [19.08, 29.21]; Greedy-DiM-S 6.93 → 29.41, +22.47 [18.00, 27.43]. <strong>Regular:</strong> not tested under a registered rule (descriptive: AMSL 15.1 → 28.9, WebMorph 4.9 → 10.8). <strong>GAN:</strong> C3 absence (Status). Renders vs camera 0.947 / 0.980 / 0.964.</td>
<td>Diffusion: MorDIFF (C2 cell); DiM-C and Greedy-DiM-S (descriptive)</td>
<td>MorDIFF 4.9 → 19.6, +14.7 [10.3, 18.9]; d′ share 0.463 &lt; 0.5. Tier 2 not reached: p10 0.0170 &gt; its Holm level 0.00833 (the printed interval starts at 10.3, but the rule is the one-sided test). A rise in all five crops (+13.2 to +21.0). <strong>Not met.</strong></td>
<td>FRLL FaceMorpher under E7 4.42 [2.12, 6.93] (F4 (ii) supported). But the MorDIFF control moves the ViT-L/14 release by +10.74 [7.22, 14.19]; in the central 256-px window that rise stays at +12.3 [6.6, 16.2] (A42, post hoc; CONCLUSIONS: the non-specificity "is not a border artefact"). <strong>Not shown for MorDIFF.</strong></td>
<td><strong>Not met:</strong> the registered refuter fired (F7, H-new-139b, falsified by its kill): MorDIFF morphs vs reconstructions 0.847 [0.803, 0.891]. With border area matched: 0.844 [0.787, 0.895] (A42, post hoc). Central 256-px window: 0.61 [0.56, 0.65] (A42 amendment 1, post hoc, explanation only; not a border test). DiM-A 0.361 the other way (descriptive). Identity evidence or a file/frame property: open.</td>
<td><strong>Met as registered</strong> (F6 supported; five crops of our frames, not raw files). No raw-file run with MADation's pipeline. On our frames MorDIFF 4.9 against a published 1.1.</td>
<td><strong>C2 "descriptive row (final)"</strong> (a registered refuter fired). Earlier registered test (A36 H-new-75): "neither". GAN: C3 absence, "strong (narrow)"; not a shortcut grade. H1 <code>orig</code> "above" (registered label, no grade).</td>
<td>A42 amendment 1: read (post hoc; see "Beside C2" in §4). A43 (the MorDIFF two-by-two, H-new-241; staged, not registered): pending. Then off-centre same-scale windows (H-new-262/263, proposed, not registered), a MorDIFF fidelity check, a fresh-data replication (H-new-234).</td>
</tr>
